<!--
  RM_Miasma_ArthropodFloor.xml                       MIASMA_FAUNA_FLOOR_ROSTER_1

  The remaining three of the arthropod floor's four scuttlers
  (miasma_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md §2): RM_Karravel (the carpet),
  RM_Karrimeth (the mass), RM_Karrolun (the harvest). The fourth,
  the delta-loam composter, already ships as RUT_Karrobel
  (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_Karrobel.xml,
  COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1) — built before this item claimed, from the
  same roster document, and left in its existing RUT_ tier rather than
  moved (renaming a def other art jobs already reference by name is out of
  this item's scope). These three are new-this-pass and land directly in
  RM_Miasma (this mod now exists, unlike when Karrobel/Karrathil shipped),
  so they ship RM_-tier per Q11a from the start.

  🔑 One population, four draws on it (roster §2's own load-bearing note):
  all four scuttlers — these three plus RUT_Karrobel — share
  RM_VerminPressureExtension's populationGroupTag "RM_MiasmaScuttlers" and
  carry RM_CompProperties_VerminBreeder, so the shared
  RM_MapComponent_VerminPopulation/RM_CompVerminBreeder pairing
  (src/RimMandrake/CreatureBehaviors/Source/, mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors)
  tracks and replenishes them as one pool against predation by the five
  RM_Miasma_Predators.xml plants, the nursery juveniles, refugee predators
  and the RM_Karrolun harvest — exactly the mechanism the roster names
  ("there is already a mechanism for exactly this") rather than inventing a
  new one. RUT_Karrobel.xml is retrofitted with the same comp/extension in
  this same pass so all four actually share one pool, not three sharing and
  a fourth silently outside it.

  Bodies reuse the two shapes this campaign's karr- clade already
  established (RUT_Karrobel.xml/RUT_Karrathil.xml): BeetleLike for a small
  ambient scuttler, BeetleLikeWithClaw where the roster calls for a bigger,
  gripping/blade-bearing animal. No new BodyDef — none of the three
  silhouettes (disc, mass-of-small, big-and-long-limbed) needs a bespoke
  body, only distinct stats/graphics/wildGroupSize per the roster's own
  "each one's silhouette follows its job, not its family."

  🔑 Two of these three "must not be briefed as hero sprites" (roster §7):
  RM_Karravel has to read as a carpet and RM_Karrimeth only ever as a mass.
  No new C# for that — same idiom already used for RUT_Karrathil's swarm
  ("a HIGH wildGroupSize on an otherwise ordinary small-insect PawnKindDef...
  no new C# needed for reads as a haze in numbers"): both get deliberately
  high, INVENTED wildGroupSize instead of a bespoke rendering mechanism.

  Art: genuinely new, none exists — checked infrastructure/artpipe/
  {done,pending,active,failed}, _artsrc, registry.jsonl by all three names
  and by "scuttler"/"carpet"/"mass" first, clean. Flat-color placeholders
  shipped this pass (south-facing only, matching the RUT_Karrobel/
  RUT_Karrathil precedent of a single low ground pose for a "mostly seen as
  a mass/carpet/half-buried" creature) so the mod loads clean; no fresh
  fill_queue.py job filed this pass — a hero-sprite brief would deliver the
  wrong thing for two of the three per the caution above, and the third
  (Karrolun) is ordinary but not urgent enough on its own to file solo. Real
  art is follow-on work, same posture RUT_Karrobel/RUT_Karrathil are
  already sitting in (their own jobs FAILED and are unconsumed in
  infrastructure/artpipe/pending — a pre-existing gap this item does not
  own or attempt to fix).

  Predation onto these three (and onto RUT_Karrobel) by the five
  RM_Miasma_Predators.xml plants is NOT built here — that plant file's own
  header already defers it as a genuine engine question ("can a plant
  consume a small wild animal at all, and can it be restricted to one
  species") UNMEASURABLE on the Mac, and this pass does not reason it out
  from a doc either. The prey now exists; the predation comp is follow-on,
  Desktop-gated work.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ==================== RM_Karravel — the carpet ==================== -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Karravel</defName>
    <label>karravel</label>
    <description>A coin-flat armoured disc the size of a palm, dull olive with a fine salt bloom, its legs never showing beneath the shell. Alone it is nothing. In numbers — and karravel are never anything but numerous — they cover the mud film so completely the ground itself appears to be sliding. The Miasma's cheapest protein, and the bulk of everything that eats here.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.9</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>0.4</Mass>
      <MarketValue>6</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.2</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>18</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>58</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.15</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.05</ArmorRating_Blunt>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandibles</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>2</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Mouth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.3</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>BeetleLike</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <baseBodySize>0.18</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.4</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.4</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <fleshType>Insectoid</fleshType>
      <bloodDef>Filth_BloodInsect</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <meatColor>(150,140,120)</meatColor>
      <meatMarketValue>0.2</meatMarketValue>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <roamMtbDays>3</roamMtbDays>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.01</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.01</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>3</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>3</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1.4)</li>
          <li>(2.5, 1.8)</li>
          <li>(3, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.1</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.3</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Insectoid_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompProperties_VerminBreeder" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors">
        <pawnSpawnIntervalDays>0.5~1</pawnSpawnIntervalDays>
        <pawnSpawnRadius>3</pawnSpawnRadius>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_VerminPressureExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors">
        <populationSoftCap>40</populationSoftCap>
        <populationHardCap>100</populationHardCap>
        <populationGroupTag>RM_MiasmaScuttlers</populationGroupTag>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Karravel</defName>
    <label>karravel</label>
    <race>RM_Karravel</race>
    <combatPower>3</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>8~24</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.9</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Karravel/RM_Karravel</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.35</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Karravel/RM_Karravel</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.45</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
